.TH DIPIXMLTV 1 "2026-08-27" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipixmltv \- convert between XMLTV and the DVB-IPI EPG (TVA) XML shape
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipixmltv
\fB\-f\fR xmltv \fB\-M\fR \fImap\fR [\fB\-i\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dipixmltv
\fB\-f\fR tva [\fB\-R\fR \fIrevmap\fR] [\fB\-i\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dipixmltv
\fB\-S\fR \fIscan.csv\fR [\fB\-i\fR \fIguide.xml\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIpath\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipixmltv
converts between xmltv guide data and the plain (non-BiM) DVB-IPI EPG XML
shape (TVA metadata, ETSI TS 102 822-3-1/-3-2). XMLTV itself is not part
of DVB-IPI; TVA XML is. \fB\-f\fR names the \fIinput\fR format, the other
direction is always produced: \fB\-f xmltv\fR reads xmltv and writes
TVA-shaped XML, \fB\-f tva\fR reads TVA-shaped XML and writes xmltv.
.PP
xmltv channel ids carry no DVB identity, and the tsid/onid/sid triplet
from a dipiscan scan is commonly degenerate across services on the same
headend (every service reporting tsid=1 onid=0 sid=1 is normal).
Conversion is therefore keyed on the multicast URI, the one part
guaranteed unique per service. \fB\-M\fR supplies the id-to-URI/triplet
mapping required for \fB\-f xmltv\fR; an xmltv channel with no entry in
the map is silently dropped, along with its programmes. \fB\-R\fR
optionally renames an incoming TVA serviceId back to a preferred local
xmltv id when converting the other way; without it the incoming
serviceId is kept as-is.
.PP
With \fB\-S\fR, instead of converting, \fBdipixmltv\fR reads a dipiscan
CSV capture and an xmltv guide, and writes a suggested \fB\-M\fR mapping
to \fB\-o\fR. Channels are matched by every \fB<display\-name>\fR, not
just the first: an exact case-insensitive match becomes a live mapping
line; a substring match becomes a \fB#\fR-commented line with the
closest guess, for you to confirm or fix; no match at all becomes
\fB# UNMATCHED: \fIid\fR (\fIname\fR)\fR. Review the result before use
as \fB\-M\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " \fIpath\fR"
Input path, "\-" for stdin (default).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIpath\fR"
Output path, "\-" for stdout (default).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIfmt\fR"
Names the INPUT format: \fBxmltv\fR or \fBtva\fR. Output is always the
other one. Required unless \fB\-S\fR is given.
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-map " \fIpath\fR"
Channel map, one \fIid\fR,\fIuri\fR,\fItsid\fR,\fIonid\fR,\fIsid\fR line
per channel: dipiscan's own csv shape, with column 1 repurposed to the
xmltv channel id. Required for \fB\-f xmltv\fR.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-reverse\-map " \fIrevmap\fR"
Reverse map, one \fIuri\fR,\fIid\fR line per channel. Optional, used
only with \fB\-f tva\fR.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-suggest\-map " \fIpath\fR"
Switch to suggest-map mode: read a dipiscan csv from \fIpath\fR and an
xmltv guide from \fB\-i\fR, write a suggested \fB\-M\fR mapping to
\fB\-o\fR. See DESCRIPTION for the matching rules. \fB\-f\fR is not
required in this mode.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print one summary line to stderr: channels and programmes read. No
effect with \fB\-S\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
auto|always|never (default auto).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH XMLTV CONFORMANCE
Output aims to be DTD-valid xmltv: \fBdisplay\-name\fR and \fBtitle\fR
are required non-empty elements in xmltv.dtd, so a channel with no
source name falls back to its id, and a programme with no title falls
back to \fB(untitled)\fR.
.PP
The reader is lenient: a conforming file always works, and quirks
outside the DTD that don't touch the fields dipixmltv needs are not
rejected either.
.SH CRIDS
TVA's \fBprogramId\fR/\fBcrid\fR is a constrained \fBanyURI\fR
(\fBcrid://.../...\fR); raw xmltv ids, which can contain anything, are
not valid there directly, and the tsid/onid/sid triplet is too often
degenerate to use as a collision-free key. \fBdipixmltv\fR builds the
CRID from the xmltv channel id instead, which is unique within its own
source:
.PP
.nf
.RS
crid://dipixmltv.invalid/\fI<percent\-encoded\-channel\-id>\fR/\fI<programme\-start\-timestamp>\fR
.RE
.fi
.PP
\fBdipixmltv.invalid\fR is not a registered CRID authority; the
\fB.invalid\fR TLD is reserved for this under RFC 2606. Because the
timestamp is part of the id, a rescheduled programme gets a new CRID.
Do not use this id as a hard reference in a PVR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipixmltv \-f xmltv \-M mapping.csv \-i guide.xml \-o guide.tva.xml
Convert xmltv to TVA-shaped XML using an explicit channel mapping.
.TP
.B dipixmltv \-f tva \-i guide.tva.xml \-o guide.xml
Convert TVA-shaped XML back to xmltv.
.TP
.B dipixmltv \-S scan.csv \-i guide.xml \-o mapping.csv
Build a suggested \fB\-M\fR mapping from a dipiscan CSV capture and an
xmltv guide, matched by display name.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B nonzero
Argument error, or I/O failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipibcg (1),
.BR dipibim (1),
.BR dipiscan (1)
.PP
